**Expressing $x$ in terms of $y$:**
We isolate $x$ on one side of the equation:
\begin{align*}
x + 3y &= 3 \\
x &= 3 - 3y
\end{align*}
So when $y$ is expressed in terms of $x$, $x = \boxed{3 - 3y}$.

**Expressing $y$ in terms of $x$:**
Now, we solve for $y$:
\begin{align*}
x + 3y &= 3 \\
3y &= 3 - x \\
y &= \frac{3 - x}{3}
\end{align*}
So when $x$ is expressed in terms of $y$, $y = \boxed{\frac{3 - x}{3}}$.

